{% extends "tutorial_base.html.j2" %}

{% block tutorial_body %}
        <!-- Intro Card -->
        <div class="doc-intro-card">
          <h2>Dial In Pierces, Holding Tabs &amp; Nest Layouts Directly on the Canvas</h2>
          <p>
            Auto-nesting covers most jobs, yet real plate and tube work still calls for quick shop tweaks. Move a pierce away from a tight flange, pin a small bracket with a holding tab, spin a gusset around plate rust, or flip a tube end-for-end without reopening CAD.
          </p>
          <div class="doc-intro-grid">
            <div class="doc-intro-stat">
              <span class="label">Contour Tweaks</span>
              <span class="value">Move Pierce &amp; Edit Tabs</span>
            </div>
            <div class="doc-intro-stat">
              <span class="label">2D Sheet Nest</span>
              <span class="value">&Delta;X/&Delta;Y Drag, 15&deg; Rotate &amp; Halos</span>
            </div>
            <div class="doc-intro-stat">
              <span class="label">1D Stick Strip</span>
              <span class="value">Reorder, 180&deg; Flip &amp; &Delta;A Roll</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 1
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-1">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 01</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Move Your Pierce Point (<code class="mono">Move Pierce</code>, <code class="mono">Maker</code> &amp; <code class="mono">Pro Shop</code>)</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              Put pierce craters inside your scrap slug and keep them away from bolt-hole walls:
            </p>
            <ul class="doc-bullet-list">
              <li>Click <span class="ui-chip cyan">Move Pierce</span> above the 3D preview (next to <span class="ui-chip">Inspect</span> and <span class="ui-chip">Edit Tabs</span>).</li>
              <li>Click or drag along a contour in the 3D preview or 2D map to slide the green and red lead-in markers into scrap.</li>
              <li>Your lead-ins and lead-outs update automatically for Single-File and Pack Mode. Click <span class="ui-chip">Reset Auto Pierce</span> to revert, or <span class="ui-chip">Done</span> to lock it in.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <figure class="doc-figure">
            <div class="doc-figure-bar">
              <span class="doc-figure-caption"><span class="dot"></span> Step 1: Move Pierce editor with 3D marker preview and Reset Auto Pierce</span>
              <span class="doc-figure-zoom">🔍 Click image to enlarge</span>
            </div>
            <div class="doc-figure-img-wrap">
              <picture>
                <source srcset="assets/v08-move-pierce.webp" type="image/webp" />
                <img src="assets/v08-move-pierce.png" alt="Step 1: Move Pierce mode with 2D contour drag and 3D pierce preview" width="2880" height="1800" loading="lazy" />
              </picture>
            </div>
          </figure>
        </article>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 2
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-2">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 02</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Add Holding Tabs (<code class="mono">Edit Tabs</code>, <code class="mono">Pro Shop</code>)</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              Stop small cutouts and thin brackets from tipping on the slats or dropping into your chuck mid-cut:
            </p>
            <ul class="doc-bullet-list">
              <li>Click <span class="ui-chip cyan">Edit Tabs</span> above the 3D preview (or <span class="ui-chip">Edit Tabs on Canvas</span> inside a contour's settings).</li>
              <li>Click any contour edge to drop a holding tab. Drag tabs along the cut line to clear weld seams and machined faces.</li>
              <li><code class="mono">Shift-Click</code> or click the tab's <code class="mono">&times;</code> button to remove it. Your kerf-compensated bridge stays uncut so parts stay anchored until you snap them free.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <figure class="doc-figure">
            <div class="doc-figure-bar">
              <span class="doc-figure-caption"><span class="dot"></span> Step 2: Edit Tabs mode with contour tab placement and posted G-code</span>
              <span class="doc-figure-zoom">🔍 Click image to enlarge</span>
            </div>
            <div class="doc-figure-img-wrap">
              <picture>
                <source srcset="assets/v08-edit-tabs.webp" type="image/webp" />
                <img src="assets/v08-edit-tabs.png" alt="Step 2: Edit Tabs holding tab placement with contour editor and G-code panel" width="2880" height="1800" loading="lazy" />
              </picture>
            </div>
          </figure>
        </article>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 3
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-3">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 03</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Drag, Rotate <code class="mono">15&deg;</code> &amp; Flip Nested Sheet Parts</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              Adjust flat-plate nests right inside <span class="ui-chip">Stock Nesting</span> without typing coordinates:
            </p>
            <ul class="doc-bullet-list">
              <li>Pick <span class="ui-chip cyan">Select / Move</span> on the 2D sheet canvas and drag any part in <code class="mono">&Delta;X, &Delta;Y</code>.</li>
              <li>Rotate parts in <code class="mono">15&deg;</code> steps or free angles. Flip horizontally (<code class="mono">X</code>) or vertically (<code class="mono">Y</code>) to tuck gussets or dodge rusted plate.</li>
              <li>Check green and red spacing and edge halos before posting G-code. Click <span class="ui-chip">Reset Auto-Nest</span> anytime to restore the auto-nest layout (<code class="mono">Maker &le; 5 parts</code>, <code class="mono">Pro Shop unlimited</code>).</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <figure class="doc-figure">
            <div class="doc-figure-bar">
              <span class="doc-figure-caption"><span class="dot"></span> Step 3: 2D sheet Select / Move controls for drag, 15-degree rotation, and flip</span>
              <span class="doc-figure-zoom">🔍 Click image to enlarge</span>
            </div>
            <div class="doc-figure-img-wrap">
              <picture>
                <source srcset="assets/v08-2d-sheet-interact.webp" type="image/webp" />
                <img src="assets/v08-2d-sheet-interact.png" alt="Step 3: 2D sheet Select / Move transform HUD with X/Y move, 15-degree rotate, and flip" width="2880" height="1800" loading="lazy" />
              </picture>
            </div>
          </figure>
        </article>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 4
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-4">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 04</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Reorder, Flip <code class="mono">180&deg;</code> &amp; Roll <code class="mono">&Delta;A</code> on Rotary Sticks</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              Tune multi-part tube packing along each stick in rotary Pack Mode:
            </p>
            <ul class="doc-bullet-list">
              <li>Reorder tubes along the 1D stick strip so short drops sit near the tailstock and heavy parts stay near the chuck.</li>
              <li>Flip parts <code class="mono">180&deg;</code> end-for-end and roll phase angle <code class="mono">&Delta;A</code> to point copes and miters for clean torch clearance.</li>
              <li>Set part-to-part cut gap per stick while keeping compatible <code class="mono">Common-Line</code> sever cuts intact.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <figure class="doc-figure">
            <div class="doc-figure-bar">
              <span class="doc-figure-caption"><span class="dot"></span> Step 4: 1D rotary stick strip controls for reorder, 180-degree flip, and phase roll</span>
              <span class="doc-figure-zoom">🔍 Click image to enlarge</span>
            </div>
            <div class="doc-figure-img-wrap">
              <picture>
                <source srcset="assets/v08-1d-stick-controls.webp" type="image/webp" />
                <img src="assets/v08-1d-stick-controls.png" alt="Step 4: Stock Nesting 1D rotary stick controls with reorder, 180 flip, and delta A roll" width="2880" height="1800" loading="lazy" />
              </picture>
            </div>
          </figure>
        </article>
{% endblock %}
